    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our highest-rated asset at 72.64. The combination of his power profile and a favorable matchup against Ray, who carries a shaky 4.95 xERA, makes him an elite play. We also see high-ceiling value from **Jonathan Aranda** (64.59) and **Dylan Beavers** (63.81). **Jonathan Aranda** is particularly well-positioned; his dynamic platoon edge (+12%) against Gray and a prime #2 spot in the order maximizes his run-scoring potential. Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** benefits from a strong platoon setup, giving him the statistical edge to capitalize on Brown\u2019s 4.53 xERA. While **Masyn Winn** sits at 61.65, he remains a critical component of our strategy due to the 85% stolen base success rate against the opposing battery, providing that crucial speed dimension we prioritize in the 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Tyler Freeman**, whose 46.09 score nearly warranted a start. Ultimately, he was sidelined in favor of the higher-efficiency projections offered by **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Masyn Winn**, both of whom benefit from more favorable lineup positioning. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding **Bryce Harper** and **Daulton Varsho**; although they are in the lineup, they face elite arms in McLean (3.49 xERA) and Burke (3.57 xERA) respectively, which drags their daily scores into the marginal 55\u201357 range. We are also monitoring the status of **Will Smith** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remain on the IL, limiting our depth as we navigate this stretch. With no major weather concerns currently flagged, our primary goal is to maximize the efficiency of our speed-heavy roster against these mid-tier starters.",
